; Example — Marposs touch probe workpiece Z touch-off, then zero G54 Z there.
;
; This is a template to copy/adapt, not auto-loaded by anything. Run it from
; MDI or load it standalone before running a Fusion-generated program, or
; paste the relevant lines into a Fusion 360 "Manual NC" block — see
; README.md "Probing from Fusion 360".
;
; Position X/Y over the point you want to probe (by hand or a preceding
; rapid move) before running this — it only probes in Z.

M107                      ; deploy the Marposs probe
G38.2 Z-50 F100           ; probe down; G38.2 aborts the program if it never
                          ; triggers before Z-50, so no separate check needed
#<touch_z> = #5063        ; Z position where the probe tripped
G0 Z[#<touch_z> + 5]      ; retract clear before stowing the probe
M108                      ; retract the Marposs probe
G10 L20 P1 Z0             ; set G54 Z0 at the touched surface

; #5063 needs verification against your installed LinuxCNC version (same
; caveat as remap/m106_remap.ngc). Feed, start height, and probe distance
; above are placeholders — adjust for your actual stock/setup.
